  "body": "## What changed\n\nA post script for Grbl 1.1 3-axis mills, and a machine for it.\n\n- `assets/posts/grbl.cps` (new). Derived from our `grblhal.cps`. Grbl 1.1 has no canned cycles, no cutter radius compensation and no tool table, so:\n  - Drill cycles post as G0/G1/G4 moves. The engine already sends the expanded hole moves, and the script passes them through (as `tinyg.cps` does). A dwell (P > 0) is a G4 at the hole bottom.\n  - BORE and TAP are refused by name. An expanded bore needs a spindle stop before the rapid retract; a tap needs a synchronised spindle.\n  - A tool change is a retract, a comment `(TOOL CHANGE - LOAD T<n> - SET Z ZERO - RESUME)` and `M0`. The first tool gets `(LOAD T<n> AND SET Z ZERO BEFORE THE START)`. No M6, no G43/G49.\n  - G41/G42 control compensation is refused, as on TinyG.\n  - A line is at most 79 characters (the Grbl 1.1 line buffer is 80 bytes with the terminator). A comment is cut to fit. A motion line that does not fit refuses the program.\n- `assets/machines/grbl-3axis.mch` (new): a copy of `grblhal-3axis.mch`, model \"Grbl 3-axis\".\n- `crates/app/src/posting_files.rs`: the post \"Grbl 1.1\" after TinyG, the machine \"Grbl 3-axis\", and their embedded copies.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `drill_peck.nc`: `(LOAD T4 AND SET Z ZERO BEFORE THE START)`, then G0/G1 pecks to Z-24 and a G0 retract. No G8x word.\n- Longest line over all Grbl NC goldens: 43 characters.\n- Refusal goldens (`crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/grbl/*.refusal`): rotary, C-axis live tool, probe and thread hand are refused by name.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/post/tests/script_grbl.rs` (new): `post_suite!(\"grbl.cps\")` with its recorded goldens.\n- `crates/post/tests/grbl_dialect.rs` (new): every line of every Grbl golden is at most 79 characters and has none of G73, G81-G89, G98, G99, G41, G42, G43, M6, O or H words.\n- `grbl` added to the shared post tables: `conformance`, `post_spindle_rule_all`, `machine`, `first_traverse_clearance`, `end_units`, `declared_options`, `expanded_bore_refusal` (new test `grbl_refuses_expanded_bore`), post and app `bore_cycle`, `comment_escape`, `comp`, `control_comp`, `wear_comp`, `program_units`, `after_op`, `fanuc_post`.\n- `first_traverse_clearance.rs`: new helper `is_tool_change` reads M6 or the two Grbl tool comments as a tool change.\n- App goldens: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/grbl/*` and `synth_grbl.nc`, written with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`.\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` with the worktree's own target dir: 624 steps, 1 failed. The failure is `microarc_test_part::a_wrapped_op_on_the_test_part_posts_wrapped_a` (Tormach golden line count 3246 != 3245). This PR does not touch the Tormach post. It is the known red main in #2483 (caused by #2386).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No reading on a real Grbl 1.1 control and no air cut.\n- Grbl 1.1 receives G-code from a sender program. The sender's own limits are not checked.\n\n## Decision\n\n`docs/decisions/2481-grbl-post.md`.\n\nChangelog: New post \"Grbl 1.1\" and machine \"Grbl 3-axis\": drill cycles as plain moves, tool change as M0, bore, tap and G41/G42 refused, lines of 79 characters or less.\n\nFixes #2481\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
